{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2960,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've come to Caltech because there is a\nbrand new gravitational wave discovery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7460,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go find out what it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14420,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can we talk about the discovery, Rana?\n-Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17580,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can I-- I want to sit on one of my black holes.\n-Alright."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21480,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you notice, this one's a big one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24980,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that one's a little one.\n-This one is a little one.\n-Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29540,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I-I always feel like I'm the most excited out of everybody."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31300,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Really?\n-Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32800,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because excited when nothing's happening.\nCleaning some dust off a piece of glass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36600,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it still seems exciting, because I think\nthis is the key piece of glass in our"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40170,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system and I'm just clean dust off of it.\nHow cool is that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43140,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On January 4th,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44520,
    "dDurationMs": 6510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like a few hours after midnight.\nBoom. We got another signal much like the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51030,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first signal we found in September of\n2015. And it's also well represented by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56910,
    "dDurationMs": 5309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these black holes that we're sitting on.\nOne of the black holes had a mass of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62219,
    "dDurationMs": 7141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 30 solar masses and the other one\nwas about 20. And this one lasted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69360,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "longer than the first one. Both because\nour detectors are better at the lowest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73950,
    "dDurationMs": 5910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frequencies and because the signal is\nfrom black holes which are smaller, so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79860,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they last longer. And it's really\ndramatic if you listen to the audio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84780,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first signal that we got, it's only\naudible for about a tenth of a second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88680,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just, \"boomp,\" like this. But this new\none sounds like \"bvoom.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93820,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a little bit more drawn-out and it comes from\nfarther away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98140,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the furthest black hole merger that we've been\nable to detect. So it's about three billion light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103560,
    "dDurationMs": 3809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years away, which means that signal-- the\nmerger actually happened three billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107369,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years ago and the signal has been\npropagating to us for three billion years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111180,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's particularly interesting in\nthis merger are hints that the two black"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114660,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "holes weren't spinning with the same\norientation as each other or as their orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This suggests that rather than\nforming out of binary stars, they formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "separately and later became entwined\nthrough orbital dynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126280,
    "dDurationMs": 2509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This one really says,\nokay, we now know that we're going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128789,
    "dDurationMs": 1371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be seeing a lot of these things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130160,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131310,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a relief to have another signal to know\nthat the universe is not just populated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136650,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by all tiny, tiny black holes or by no\nblack holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141100,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we improve our detector"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142470,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sensitivity by say a factor of two or\nthree, the rates will go up from, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147480,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seeing one every month or every two\nmonths to seeing one every day or every week."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151480,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would say it's very surprising\nnow that our first three signals came"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156090,
    "dDurationMs": 6660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from binary black hole mergers which,\nwere pretty much an unexpected source"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162750,
    "dDurationMs": 3110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as of mid-2015."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165860,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a working theory --\nkind of exotic -- that says that some of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168750,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the black holes we're seeing are\nprimordial, alright? They weren't formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171510,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through, you know, conventional supernova\nexplosions. They were formed during the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175380,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Big Bang themselves. And they could be a\npart of Dark Matter, component of dark matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180640,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we may actually\ndetermine after we get statistics on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184050,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lots and lots and lots of these black\nhole mergers that we're actually seeing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187950,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe a hint of dark matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189860,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's sort of\nscratching at the door of the biggest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192660,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mysteries that we have today in\ncosmology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195580,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the past before there were any signals, \npeople used to use this phrase,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198860,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which I completely disagree with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200620,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they would say, \"you know if we don't\nfind any signals it will be even more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206540,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interesting than if we do.\"\nI said no no no no no. No no no no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211060,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lots of signals. That's what we want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213200,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now that we have a few,\nI'm feeling a little bit more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216170,
    "dDurationMs": 6550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "complacent. And so I'd say we really\nexpected to see a lot of binary neutron stars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222720,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if we don't, well isn't that interesting?\nIt means there's something going on--"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227220,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, you have all the\npieces. We already know how neutron \n stars work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230900,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've seen neutron stars\nusing radio astronomy. We know they're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234720,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out there, we know that they come\ntogether in binaries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237480,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why don't we see their gravitational waves?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239840,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it could be something else happens to them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242020,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just before the final merger and there's\nsomething in their evolutionary track"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247080,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which goes off in a different direction\nthan what we expect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250460,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think that would actually be interesting.\nI guess I've become one of those people that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254480,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "said if you don't see it then maybe it's\ninteresting, because we'll learn something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258900,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You never know how many more signals we\nhave sitting in the can that we're not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262440,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "telling you about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264600,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can you say that again?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267160,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't think so. \n-Would you give me the exclusive, Rana?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270400,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would! You know it, Derek. Come on.\nIf I had secret signals, you'd be the first to know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280360,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These lights are the\nfirst two tentacles of the jellyfish I'm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283680,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building, and there's a neural network\nwhich then drives this little chip, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288210,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "modulates these lights. And it's going to use these sensors like the proximity and the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292290,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sound to figure out if people are close\nto it. And the neural network is going to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296280,
    "dDurationMs": 6230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "train itself to flash the tentacle\nlights to make people come closer to it."
    } ]
  } ]
}
